# nr-relay-tool-delta: nothing to paste into a hot file.
#
# Cargo: every dependency the tool uses is already in native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/Cargo.toml (mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, serde_json,
#   sha2, thiserror; the tests use base64, tempfile, mixdog-testkit). No workspace member, no workspace dependency, no Cargo.lock change.
# Test target: tests/tool_renderer_delta.rs is picked up by cargo's test discovery (binary `tool_renderer_delta`); it needs no feature.
#   Verify: cargo nextest run -p mixdog-relay --features test-support --offline -E 'binary(tool_renderer_delta)'
# Fixtures: tests/fixtures/renderer-delta.recording.json is kept in the crate (as node-http-echo.recording.json is); regenerate with
#   node native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/tests/renderer_delta_record.mjs <tree>/apps/relay/deploy <scratch dir> > tests/fixtures/renderer-delta.recording.json
#   If the lead moves recordings into native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json, add this one (and its recorder) there.
# SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs): this task registers no protocol method; nothing to remove.
#
# What the callers see: `mixdog-relay renderer-delta --action=manifest --root=D` prints the manifest line;
#   `--action=create --root --delta --manifest [--base=<manifest file>]` prints the report and writes the manifest file (2-space JSON, a
#   trailing newline, the base tree hash recorded); `--action=apply --base --delta --manifest --output [--hardlink-base=true]` prints
#   {files,bytes,treeHash}. Failure: the reason on stderr, exit code 1 (Node ended in an unhandled rejection, also non-zero).
#   scripts/deploy-remote.ps1 and the VPS side call it the same way once they name the Rust binary instead of `node renderer-delta.mjs`
#   (the deploy-script task owns that edit).
